Share PostgreSQL's shared memory without System V IPC.

Unikraft implements no SysV IPC at all, so shmget() returns ENOSYS and the
server dies before it opens the database:

  FATAL:  could not create shared memory segment: Function not implemented
  DETAIL:  Failed system call was shmget(key=749, size=56, 03600).

The replacement is anonymous memory, and it is not a downgrade here: Unikraft
is a single-address-space kernel, so the postmaster and every process it
spawns share one page table. A plain anonymous mapping is therefore shared
between them by construction, at the same address, which is exactly what the
System V segment was for.

Two hunks, one per side of that: the postmaster allocates it, and the child --
which reaches this code after an execve(), so with its own globals but the same
address space -- finds it already mapped.

--- a/src/backend/port/sysv_shmem.c
+++ b/src/backend/port/sysv_shmem.c
@@ -159,6 +159,43 @@
 		int			shmget_errno = errno;
 
 		/*
+		 * There is no System V IPC in the guest kernel, so shmget() answers
+		 * ENOSYS.  The segment PostgreSQL is asking for is shared between the
+		 * postmaster and its children -- and on a single-address-space kernel
+		 * every process already shares one page table, so an ordinary
+		 * anonymous mapping is shared by construction.  Hand one back: the
+		 * postmaster's children find it at the same address (see
+		 * PGSharedMemoryReAttach below), which is what a System V segment
+		 * would have bought.
+		 *
+		 * The interlock this segment doubles as -- a second postmaster
+		 * attaching to the same data directory finds it and refuses to start
+		 * -- is vacuous rather than broken: there is one kernel and one data
+		 * directory.
+		 */
+		if (shmget_errno == ENOSYS)
+		{
+			memAddress = mmap(NULL, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
+							  PG_MMAP_FLAGS, -1, 0);
+			if (memAddress == MAP_FAILED)
+				elog(FATAL, "mmap(%zu) failed for the shared memory segment: %m",
+					 size);
+
+			/*
+			 * Keep the lockfile well-formed; the ID is meaningless without a
+			 * segment to name, so record zero.
+			 */
+			{
+				char		line[64];
+
+				sprintf(line, "%9lu %9lu", (unsigned long) memKey, 0UL);
+				AddToDataDirLockFile(LOCK_FILE_LINE_SHMEM_KEY, line);
+			}
+
+			return memAddress;
+		}
+
+		/*
 		 * Fail quietly if error indicates a collision with existing segment.
 		 * One would expect EEXIST, given that we said IPC_EXCL, but perhaps
 		 * we could get a permission violation instead?  Also, EIDRM might
@@ -890,6 +927,20 @@
 
 	elog(DEBUG3, "attaching to %p", UsedShmemSegAddr);
 	shmid = shmget(UsedShmemSegID, sizeof(PGShmemHeader), 0);
+
+	/*
+	 * With no System V IPC there is nothing to re-attach to -- and nothing to
+	 * do.  This kernel has a single address space shared by every process, so
+	 * the segment the postmaster allocated above is already mapped here, at
+	 * the very address it passed down in UsedShmemSegAddr.
+	 */
+	if (shmid < 0 && errno == ENOSYS)
+	{
+		hdr = (PGShmemHeader *) UsedShmemSegAddr;
+		dsm_set_control_handle(hdr->dsm_control);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (shmid < 0)
 		state = SHMSTATE_FOREIGN;
 	else
